  "live_records": {
    "q-114356": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114356",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{7x}{7x+2}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{7x+2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add and subtract $2$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x}{7x+2}=\\frac{7x+2-2}{7x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+2-2}{7x+2} & =\\frac{7x+2}{7x+2}+\\frac{-2}{7x+2} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-2}{7x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=-2,$ and we get \n\n$$\na+b=1+(-2)=-1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
