    "q-88259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88259",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{2{x}^{2}-3},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we subtract and add $3$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3+3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3+3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3}{2{x}^{2}-3}+\\frac{3+1}{2{x}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{4}{2{x}^{2}-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=4,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=1+4=5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
