    "q-114371": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114371",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{2}+x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{{x}^{2}+x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b+c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+10}{{x}^{2}+x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{{x}^{2}+x}+\\frac{-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-x+10}{{x}^{2}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=10,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-1)+10=10.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
