    "q-114378": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114378",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Write $\\frac{35{x}^{4}}{7{x}^{3}+2}$ in the form $ax+\\frac{bx}{7{x}^{3}+2},$ where $a\\ne 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator to put $7{x}^{3}$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $2$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{35{x}^{4}}{7{x}^{3}+2} & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3})}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2-2)}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)+5x(-2)}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2} & =\\frac{5x(7{x}^{3}+2)}{7{x}^{3}+2}+\\frac{-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2} \\\\  & =5x+\\frac{-10x}{7{x}^{3}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=5$ and $b=-10,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=5+(-10)=-5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
